 "content": "**The Keeper and the Storm**\n\nAn old lighthouse keeper named Maren tended her lamp for forty years. One night, a violent storm smashed the fishing village's boats, and the villagers came to her door, angry: \"Your light lured our ships onto the rocks!\"\n\nMaren showed them her ledger. Every night for forty years, she had recorded the weather, the tide, and her lamp's flame. That night, the entry read: *Flame lit at dusk. Wind from the north. I warned the harbor at sunset that no boat should sail.*\n\n\"But we didn't listen to the warnings,\" the villagers admitted. \"We blamed your light.\"\n\n**Moral: A guiding light cannot save those who ignore it; people often blame the beacon for their own closed eyes.**"
}